{"qid":"Q1483495","names":["Principality of Smolensk"],"title":"Principality of Smolensk","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Principality of Smolensk was a Rurikid appanage centered on the upper Dnieper city of Smolensk, first assigned as a dependency of Kiev in 1054 and elevated to an independent principality under Rostislav Mstislavich around 1125, whose descendants (the Rostislavichi) held the throne for nearly three centuries. At its twelfth-century peak the principality controlled a broad swathe of the upper Dnieper and Dvina drainage, with princes of Smolensk intermittently seizing the Kievan throne and building durable ties to Novgorod and Riga through Hanseatic trade. Fragmented by appanage division and devastated by Mongol campaigns, the principality was absorbed into the Grand Duchy of Lithuania when Vytautas the Great captured Smolensk in 1404, ending the reign of its last prince Yury.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. General territorial outline is known from chronicles, but internal boundary changes among appanage sub-principalities are poorly documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Smolensk","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Smolensk"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Principality of Smolensk","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Smolensk"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Principality of Smolensk","rulers":[{"qid":"Q4130535","name":"Vyacheslav Yaroslavich","nativeName":"Вячеслав Ярославич","roman":"Vyacheslav Yaroslavich","start":1054,"end":1057,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":"Q4197646","name":"Igor Yaroslavich","nativeName":